  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "368a6ddc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2 — Create the `CSVReader` Class\n",
    "\n",
    "The class contains:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `__init__(file_path)` → stores the CSV file path.\n",
    "- `read()` → reads the CSV file using pandas.\n",
    "- `preview(n)` → prints the first `n` rows.\n",
    "\n",
    "`self.data` stores the loaded DataFrame so other methods can reuse it.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "f67b5b70",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.100003Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.099870Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.105699Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.104959Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class CSVReader:\n",
    "    \"\"\"A simple reusable class for reading and previewing CSV files.\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    def __init__(self, file_path):\n",
    "        \"\"\"Store the CSV file path.\"\"\"\n",
    "        self.file_path = file_path\n",
    "        self.data = None\n",
    "\n",
    "    def read(self):\n",
    "        \"\"\"Read the CSV file and store it in self.data.\"\"\"\n",
    "        self.data = pd.read_csv(self.file_path)\n",
    "        return self.data\n",
    "\n",
    "    def preview(self, n=5):\n",
    "        \"\"\"Print the first n rows of the loaded CSV file.\"\"\"\n",
    "        if self.data is None:\n",
    "            self.read()\n",
    "\n",
    "        print(self.data.head(n))"
   ]
  },
