    "# Exercise 2: Strategy Pattern for Missing Values\n",
    "\n",
    "### Objective\n",
    "\n",
    "This exercise introduces the **Strategy Pattern**.\n",
    "\n",
    "We will create:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `MissingValueStrategy` → abstract parent class\n",
    "- `DropMissing` → removes rows with missing values\n",
    "- `FillMean` → fills numeric missing values with the mean\n",
    "- `FillMode` → fills missing values with the most frequent value\n",
    "- `DataCleaner` → applies the selected strategy\n",
    "\n",
    "The Strategy Pattern lets us change the cleaning method without changing `DataCleaner`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "219f8f66",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1 — Import Abstract Base Class Tools\n",
    "\n",
    "`ABC` means **Abstract Base Class**.\n",
    "\n",
    "`@abstractmethod` defines a method that subclasses must implement.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "7558ea03",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.163144Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.163014Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.166165Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.165138Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from abc import ABC, abstractmethod"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "defc9b60",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
