   "source": [
    "## 3 — Create the Abstract Strategy Class\n",
    "\n",
    "Every missing-value strategy will use the same method name: `handle(df)`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "id": "203d76f8",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.174026Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.173897Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.179451Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.178421Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class MissingValueStrategy(ABC):\n",
    "\n",
    "    @abstractmethod\n",
    "    def handle(self, df):\n",
    "        pass"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8c34ba8b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4 — Create `DropMissing`\n",
    "\n",
    "This strategy removes rows that contain missing values.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "fbe1eb69",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.191413Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.191248Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.195792Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.195174Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class DropMissing(MissingValueStrategy):\n",
    "\n",
    "    def handle(self, df):\n",
    "        return df.dropna()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5a18d168",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5 — Create `FillMean`\n",
    "\n",
    "This strategy fills missing values in numeric columns using the column mean.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "a5c471d6",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.197480Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.197291Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.201613Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.201075Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class FillMean(MissingValueStrategy):\n",
    "\n",
    "    def handle(self, df):\n",
    "        df = df.copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "        numeric_columns = df.select_dtypes(include=\"number\").columns\n",
    "\n",
    "        for column in numeric_columns:\n",
    "            df[column] = df[column].fillna(df[column].mean())\n",
    "\n",
    "        return df"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c543f7bb",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6 — Create `FillMode`\n",
    "\n",
    "The **mode** is the most frequent value in a column.\n",
    "\n",
    "This strategy can work with both numeric and text columns.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "b8d26a5b",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.204714Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.204603Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.210897Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.209143Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class FillMode(MissingValueStrategy):\n",
    "\n",
    "    def handle(self, df):\n",
    "        df = df.copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "        for column in df.columns:\n",
    "            if df[column].isnull().any():\n",
    "                mode_values = df[column].mode()\n",
    "\n",
    "                if not mode_values.empty:\n",
    "                    df[column] = df[column].fillna(mode_values.iloc[0])\n",
    "\n",
    "        return df"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "09285fe6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7 — Create the `DataCleaner` Class\n",
    "\n",
    "`DataCleaner` receives a strategy object and uses that strategy to clean the DataFrame.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 13,
   "id": "6d9682b7",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.212474Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.212347Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.215170Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.214648Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class DataCleaner:\n",
    "\n",
    "    def __init__(self, strategy):\n",
    "        self.strategy = strategy\n",
    "\n",
    "    def clean(self, df):\n",
    "        return self.strategy.handle(df)"
   ]
  },
  {
