   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d97f56ea",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Exercise 3: Decorators for Logging and Timing\n",
    "\n",
    "### Objective\n",
    "\n",
    "This exercise introduces the **Decorator Pattern**.\n",
    "\n",
    "We will create:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `@log_action` → prints when a method starts and finishes.\n",
    "- `@log_time` → measures execution time.\n",
    "\n",
    "A decorator adds extra behavior to a function without changing its main job.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "529909c3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1 — Import `time` and `wraps`\n",
    "\n",
    "- `time.perf_counter()` measures execution time.\n",
    "- `wraps` keeps the original function information when we decorate it.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 17,
   "id": "ec3ccbbd",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.269201Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.268869Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.272060Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.271366Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import time\n",
    "from functools import wraps"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fb99e7c1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2 — Create `log_action`\n",
    "\n",
    "This decorator prints a message before and after a function runs.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 18,
   "id": "6e9ba5a3",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.273650Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.273520Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.277050Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.276133Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def log_action(func):\n",
    "    @wraps(func)\n",
    "    def wrapper(*args, **kwargs):\n",
    "        print(f\"[START] {func.__name__}\")\n",
    "        result = func(*args, **kwargs)\n",
    "        print(f\"[END] {func.__name__}\")\n",
    "        return result\n",
    "\n",
    "    return wrapper"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4e61af25",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3 — Create `log_time`\n",
    "\n",
    "This decorator measures how long a function takes to execute.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 19,
   "id": "20f63f1b",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.278664Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.278533Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.285949Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.281620Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def log_time(func):\n",
    "    @wraps(func)\n",
    "    def wrapper(*args, **kwargs):\n",
    "        start_time = time.perf_counter()\n",
    "\n",
    "        result = func(*args, **kwargs)\n",
    "\n",
    "        end_time = time.perf_counter()\n",
    "        execution_time = end_time - start_time\n",
    "\n",
    "        print(f\"[TIME] {func.__name__}: {execution_time:.6f} seconds\")\n",
    "        return result\n",
    "\n",
    "    return wrapper"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "08240a6e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4 — Apply Decorators to `CSVReader`\n",
    "\n",
    "We redefine `CSVReader` and add decorators to the `read()` method.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 20,
   "id": "b5a13b5f",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.289455Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.289263Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.294192Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.293105Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class CSVReader:\n",
    "\n",
    "    def __init__(self, file_path):\n",
    "        self.file_path = file_path\n",
    "        self.data = None\n",
    "\n",
    "    @log_action\n",
    "    @log_time\n",
    "    def read(self):\n",
    "        self.data = pd.read_csv(self.file_path)\n",
    "        return self.data\n",
    "\n",
    "    def preview(self, n=5):\n",
    "        if self.data is None:\n",
    "            self.read()\n",
    "\n",
    "        print(self.data.head(n))"
   ]
