    "## Exercise 4 Result\n",
    "\n",
    "The factory converts a simple string into the correct transformation object:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\"normalize\"  → NormalizeColumns()\n",
    "\"duplicates\" → RemoveDuplicates()\n",
    "\"text\"       → StandardizeText()\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "This is the **Factory Pattern**.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e0e22925",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Exercise 5: Full Cleaning Pipeline — Template Method Pattern\n",
    "\n",
    "### Objective\n",
    "\n",
    "This exercise combines the previous exercises into one complete cleaning pipeline.\n",
    "\n",
    "The workflow is:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. `load()`\n",
    "2. `clean()`\n",
    "3. `transform()`\n",
    "4. `save()`\n",
    "\n",
    "The base class defines the fixed workflow, and the subclass implements each step.\n",
    "\n",
    "This is the **Template Method Pattern**.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7d2f84f6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1 — Create the Abstract `DataPipeline`\n",
    "\n",
    "The `run()` method defines the fixed sequence of the pipeline.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 33,
   "id": "6b11b161",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.512401Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.512153Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.516115Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.515211Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class DataPipeline(ABC):\n",
    "\n",
    "    def run(self):\n",
    "        self.load()\n",
    "        self.clean()\n",
    "        self.transform()\n",
    "        self.save()\n",
    "\n",
    "    @abstractmethod\n",
    "    def load(self):\n",
    "        pass\n",
    "\n",
    "    @abstractmethod\n",
    "    def clean(self):\n",
    "        pass\n",
    "\n",
    "    @abstractmethod\n",
    "    def transform(self):\n",
    "        pass\n",
    "\n",
    "    @abstractmethod\n",
    "    def save(self):\n",
    "        pass"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b60d4da7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2 — Create `CSVDataPipeline`\n",
    "\n",
    "This subclass implements each step for CSV data.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 34,
   "id": "5ed0f2ff",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.518509Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.518386Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.524281Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-22T14:29:59.523484Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class CSVDataPipeline(DataPipeline):\n",
    "\n",
    "    def __init__(\n",
    "        self,\n",
    "        input_file,\n",
    "        output_file,\n",
    "        missing_strategy,\n",
    "        transformations\n",
    "    ):\n",
    "        self.input_file = input_file\n",
    "        self.output_file = output_file\n",
    "        self.missing_strategy = missing_strategy\n",
    "        self.transformations = transformations\n",
    "        self.df = None\n",
    "\n",
    "    def load(self):\n",
    "        print(\"1. Loading data...\")\n",
    "\n",
    "        reader = CSVReader(self.input_file)\n",
    "        self.df = reader.read()\n",
    "\n",
    "        print(\"Data loaded.\")\n",
    "        print(\"Shape:\", self.df.shape)\n",
    "\n",
    "    def clean(self):\n",
    "        print(\"\\n2. Cleaning missing values...\")\n",
    "\n",
    "        cleaner = DataCleaner(self.missing_strategy)\n",
    "        self.df = cleaner.clean(self.df)\n",
    "\n",
    "        print(\"Missing values after cleaning:\")\n",
    "        print(self.df.isnull().sum())\n",
    "\n",
    "    def transform(self):\n",
    "        print(\"\\n3. Applying transformations...\")\n",
    "\n",
    "        for transform_name in self.transformations:\n",
    "            transform = TransformFactory.create_transform(transform_name)\n",
    "            self.df = transform.apply(self.df)\n",
    "\n",
    "            print(f\"Applied: {transform_name}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    def save(self):\n",
    "        print(\"\\n4. Saving cleaned data...\")\n",
    "\n",
    "        self.df.to_csv(self.output_file, index=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "        print(f\"Saved to: {self.output_file}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "533df788",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3 — Create the Pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "For this example:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `FillMean()` handles missing numeric values.\n",
    "- `\"normalize\"` cleans column names.\n",
    "- `\"duplicates\"` removes duplicate rows.\n",
    "- `\"text\"` standardizes text values.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
